==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|му́соръ||ru-PRO}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|му́сор}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-мусор.ogg}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Tatiana Kerbush-мусор.wav|a=Saint Petersburg}}

===Etymology 1===
{{uncertain|ru}}.

Per {{w|Max Vasmer|Vasmer}}, perhaps from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*meh₂d-|id=wet}}, and cognate with {{cog|grc|μύσος|t=pollution, desecration}}, {{cog|grc|μυσαρός|t=vile, covered with shame}}, {{cog|sga|mosach|t=unclean}}, {{cog|nds|mussig|t=dirty}}.

Per Preobrazhensky and {{w|Oleg Trubachyov|Trubachyov}}, cognate with dialectal terms {{m|ru|бу́сор|t=junk, old stuff}}, {{m|ru|бу́сырь}}, {{m|ru|бу́сорь}}, and probably borrowed from a {{bor|ru|trk}} language with alternation between /b/ and /m/; Trubachyov in particular characterizes Vasmer's derivation as unconvincing.

An expressive connection with {{m|ru|сор|t=rubbish, trash}} is also suggested.

